sdata> -- Issue #69's motivating case: a direct regression guard reproducing the
sdata> -- shape of issue #68 (Stmt_TABLES missing from Is_Immediate caused the REPL
sdata> -- to silently queue a bare TABLES statement as if deferred, instead of
sdata> -- running it immediately). TABLES must produce output right after being
sdata> -- typed, with no RUN in between -- if Is_Immediate ever regresses for
sdata> -- TABLES (or any other Immediate-tier statement) again, QUIT would exit
sdata> -- with no TABLES output at all and this test would fail loudly instead of
sdata> -- silently, exactly the gap #69 reports make check cannot currently catch.
sdata> USE "tests/data/freq_select.csv"
Dataset opened: tests/data/freq_select.csv
sdata> TABLES PRODUCT$
Frequency table for PRODUCT$

PRODUCT$ Frequency Percent Cum_Freq Cum_Percent
A 3 50.00 3 50.00
B 3 50.00 6 100.00
Total 6 100.00

TABLES complete.
sdata> QUIT
